# Copy to .env.development.local (pnpm dev) or .env.production.local (pnpm
# preview) to change where the demo is served. Without them, the scene and the
# panel pages use these origins (see originsFor in vite.panels.config.ts):
#
#   pnpm dev:     scene http://localhost:5173, panel pages http://localhost:5174
#   pnpm preview: scene http://localhost:4173, panel pages http://localhost:4174
#
# They must be two origins: the panel pages are on purpose another origin than
# the scene. The same variables can also be set in the environment.
VITE_HOST_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
VITE_PANEL_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5174

# The example sites under examples/sites/ that are packages of their own, each
# on its own origin (see examples/sites/vite.site.ts): by default their own
# ports, 5175-5178 with `pnpm dev:sites`, 4175-4178 with their `vp preview`.
# Set these where the sites are deployed; the scene shows them from there, and
# the sites must be built with VITE_HOST_ORIGIN set to where the scene is.
#
# To deploy, put every origin (the two above and these four) into
# .env.deploy.local and run `pnpm build:deploy` (see the README).
# VITE_SITE_WEB_STANDARDS_ORIGIN=https://web-standards.example
# VITE_SITE_HN_READER_ORIGIN=https://hn-reader.example
# VITE_SITE_CHAT_ORIGIN=https://chat.example
# VITE_SITE_GALLERY_ORIGIN=https://gallery.example
#
# The live demo (examples/live-demo) shows the sites whose origin is set here.
# Build it to deploy with VITE_HOST_ORIGIN set to where it is deployed (in the
# environment, or in .env.deploy.local): `pnpm --filter ./examples/live-demo
# build:deploy`. Build the sites it shows with the same VITE_HOST_ORIGIN.
